ECOin - DNS seeder for the ECOin network (crawler + authoritative DNS server)

===================================================

+ Build:

    make

  Requires g++ and libssl-dev (-lcrypto).

===================================================

+ Run:

    sudo ./dnsseed -p 53 -h ecoinseed.03c8.net -n ecoinseed.03c8.net -m solarnethub@riseup.net

  Port 53 needs root. The hostname given with -h must resolve to this machine,
  and UDP+TCP port 53 must be open in the firewall.

  State is kept in dnsseed.dat next to the binary. A readable snapshot of every
  known node (good flag, last success, height, services, version) is written to
  dnsseed.dump.

  Starting from an empty dnsseed.dat the crawler bootstraps from the addresses in
  mainnet_seeds (main.cpp) and discovers the rest of the network from there.

===================================================

+ Run as a service (systemd):

    /etc/systemd/system/ecoin-seeder.service

        [Unit]
        Description=ECOin DNS seeder
        After=network-online.target

        [Service]
        WorkingDirectory=/opt/ecoin-seeder
        ExecStart=/opt/ecoin-seeder/dnsseed -p 53 -h ecoinseed.03c8.net -n ecoinseed.03c8.net -m solarnethub@riseup.net
        Restart=always
        RestartSec=10

        [Install]
        WantedBy=multi-user.target

    sudo systemctl daemon-reload
    sudo systemctl enable --now ecoin-seeder

===================================================

+ Check that it works:

    dig @127.0.0.1 +short ecoinseed.03c8.net A

  It must answer with several node addresses. An empty answer means no node has
  passed validation yet: give the crawler a few minutes and check dnsseed.dump.

